TEXT -272 -208 Left 3 ;Since now the line is very long (100km)\nthe transients are very long!\nEspecially currents, active power and \nspeed of gen2 are wavering\nAlso the speed step is now less steep\nAll this is due to the high resistance of the\nline especially for such a low voltage level (20KV)\nIf the line length gets further increased\nGen2 frequency is now uncoupled to gen1\nfrequency and Gen2 is no longer controllable\nFor a working example with a 1150kV high voltage line\nbetween generator1 and generator2\nsee example Control_Range_of_speed_1000km.asc
TEXT -192 16 Left 2 ;PI-controller with\nantiwindup \nmeans: if max. limit\nof PI is reached\ncontrol is no longer\nactive
TEXT 528 192 Left 2 ;NOTE: If the line length is further increased\ngen2 will be no longer controllable
TEXT 400 232 Left 2 ;.param PN=20e6 QN=1e3
